From dd2a5c6b51f5c3fe2ade0c9ec89123ae16456971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salty-max <max@jellycat.fr>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:06:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Extract passives, tactics, equipment, teams and resolve name
 placeholders

Everything needed to feed the Kizuna bundles, on top of upstream main. The
release binary cannot produce any of this: skill parsing landed after 1.1 was
cut, and build 6.00.23.00 moved several columns.

Parsing fixes
- hissatsu: recastTime is column 18 in this build, 19 is a Byte and panicked
- common: parse_number_value, since T2B stores round numbers as Integer so a
  numeric column mixes Float and Int between rows
- text_database: write_skill never wrote description; the request channel now
  carries (name_id, description_id)

New extraction
- skills/passive.rs, tactic.rs, equipment.rs: passives moved out of
  m_skillInfoList into passive_skill_config; tactics and synergies come from
  item_config; equipment stats sit in the REGULAR_UNIQUE_BASE sub row
- characters: club affiliation from chara_base column 16

Name placeholders
- text/name_tags.rs: non-Japanese text ships <FUL:ENDO> style placeholders for
  the game to fill at runtime. chara_name_tag and map_name_tag resolve them,
  both keyed by CRC32 of the ASCII key. The prefix picks a chara_text sub
  entry, measured against Japanese and Simplified Chinese rather than assumed.
  An unresolved key aborts the process, because main.rs swallows thread panics
  and a silent fallback is what hid the problem.
- the text pipeline gained map_text, soccer_game_title and
  players_universe_text, and writes character_name_parts, place_names and
  location_names so downstream never re-reads the raw config

Tooling
- bin/: export_json and merge_db for the bundles, plus dump_schema, show_table,
  find_ids and dbstat for poking at cfg.bin files, and g4tx_to_png,
  slice_atlas, png_to_svg for the sprite atlases

Column indices are specific to build 6.00.23.00. A patch will shift them and
the symptom is a silently empty table, so check the notes in each module.
